{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-76476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/assets/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-76476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {-{C}_{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-76476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2768469284f99fdc0f2dc1edae76e46d258448cead6c2a412ee048ea1c478471"} {"question" "q-76476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-76476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-76476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/assets/3121d24ea2b9eac3d95c34202619800331d4719c786b8f5a1051350370a1bea2.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $TUVT,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ is the same path as ${C}_{1}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2768469284f99fdc0f2dc1edae76e46d258448cead6c2a412ee048ea1c478471"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] ["math" "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/assets/6087da076e65bda5240c428ff67c570ad59ae9a8e5a5a3c9e8406184998de56a.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(1,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,0)$ to the point $B(0,-2).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{7}{3},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)\\,i+(x-{y}^{2})\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the horizontal line segment from $O$ to $A.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t) & =0+t(a-0) \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+t(⟨1,0⟩-⟨0,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨t,0⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,i,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=t$ and $y=0.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =({x}^{2}+y)\\,i+(x-{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+0)\\,i+(t-{0}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0)j \\\\  & =i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =({t}^{2}\\,i+t\\,j)\\cdot (i) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2768469284f99fdc0f2dc1edae76e46d258448cead6c2a412ee048ea1c478471"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/assets/c0a4f042748ddadd824bed4ee71bca9724d7ca7dcc376a0ccf7c1353d59ec4fc.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(-2,2)$ to the point $B(-1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(-1,2)$ to the point $D(-1,0).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\frac{7}{2},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the vertical line segment from $B$ to $D.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =b+t(d-b) \\\\  & =⟨-1,2⟩+t(⟨-1,0⟩-⟨-1,2⟩) \\\\  & =⟨-1,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =-\\,i+(2-2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=-1$ and $y=2-2t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j \\\\  & =(-1-(2-2t))\\,i+(2-2t-(-1))\\,j \\\\  & =(-3+2t)\\,i+(3-2t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-2t)j \\\\  & =-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =((-3+2t)\\,i+(3-2t)\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\,j) \\\\  & =(3-2t)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4t-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t-6)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+[2{t}^{2}-6t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}+[2({1}^{2})-6(1)-0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2768469284f99fdc0f2dc1edae76e46d258448cead6c2a412ee048ea1c478471"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-\\frac{15}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-77185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{15}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-125413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+3x\\,j-4y\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-125413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-125413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2768469284f99fdc0f2dc1edae76e46d258448cead6c2a412ee048ea1c478471"} {"question" "q-125413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5678545f2b318f6737e48fbb69e9b81cc34fca90b39d00064b0b33e8bfb4832c"} {"question" "q-125413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{C}(2z+3x-4y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{C}-4y\\,\\text{d}x+2z\\,\\text{d}y+3x\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math